---
/**
 * HomepageHero — homepage hero panel (homepage-specific component).
 *
 * CLEAN-SLATE BUILD. This is a new, from-authority-only implementation of the
 * locked hero contract. It does not reuse, refactor, or inherit markup, CSS,
 * class names, spacing, typography, overlay, image crop, or layout from the
 * rejected legacy HomeHero.astro (deleted). Every decision below is derived
 * from the current approved design authority:
 *
 *   Contract:  docs/home/home-components/03-home-hero.md (exact V1 spec)
 *   Blueprint: docs/home/reference/blueprint.md §7 (Hero)
 *   Tokens:    docs/home/home-components/00-token-matrix.md
 *   Theme:     Theme V2 (Platinum) — generated/theme.css (active)
 *
 * Identity (blueprint §7): a CONTAINED CINEMATIC FEATURE PANEL. The Mercedes
 * S-Class photograph fills the entire rounded panel edge-to-edge; a
 * controlled directional overlay (semantic dark tokens via color-mix — no raw
 * rgba, no gold, no glow) protects overlaid text while keeping the car the
 * focal subject. It is NOT full-screen, NOT 100vh, NOT a centered template,
 * NOT a split with a separate image column — the image is the panel.
 *
 * Composition: PageContainer once (the contained shell) → the panel →
 * full-bleed <Image> + overlay + inner grid. Desktop 8/4 content placement
 * (left copy / right support statement) is CONTENT-PLACEMENT ONLY — it never
 * creates a separate visual image container (blueprint §7 / blueprint-to-ui
 * §18). Mobile/tablet collapse to a single reading column.
 *
 * H1 (03 §Typography / task §6 / task §8): the page's single <h1>, left-aligned,
 * on the active Theme V2 heading font (Inter Tight via --font-heading — a
 * variable face covering the full weight range). The H1 renders at the semantic
 * --font-weight-regular (400); the explicit weight overrides the UA bold default
 * — a controlled regular, not heavy/bold (task §8: avoid newspaper ultra-light
 * and marketing extra-bold extremes). Semantic h1 role (--text-h1), NOT
 * display-scale — controlled, wraps naturally, never theatrical.
 *
 * CTA hierarchy (03 §Colors / DESIGN.md §8): primary Book → <Link variant="cta">
 * (platinum fill + on-light text); secondary → <Link variant="button"> (outlined).
 * The foundation <Link> owns routing (getPath — FND-I18N-03), focus-visible,
 * 44×44 targets, and prefetch — no hero-specific button variant, no local .cta
 * classes, no client JS.
 *
 * Right-side support (blueprint §7 / 03 §Desktop): a small, restrained,
 * operational text block with a subtle divider — not cards, stats, badges, or
 * icons. Optional only because the editorial hero block does not author it yet
 * (blueprint §20); when supplied, the 7/5 split activates.
 *
 * Image / LCP (03 §Surface/image / responsive-images-performance): the hero
 * image is the page LCP, so astro:assets <Image> is used directly (the
 * foundation Image primitive types `src: string` and can't accept an imported
 * ImageMetadata — FND-IMG-08 only bans raw <img>/<picture>) with eager loading
 * + fetchpriority="high" + responsive widths/sizes. It is decorative
 * atmosphere behind the H1/copy (alt="" + role="presentation") — the title
 * carries the meaning, never copied into alt (imagery-art-direction §19).
 *
 * Motion (task §24): STATIC. No entrance animation, no background zoom/pan,
 * no parallax, no IntersectionObserver. The hero is a still composition; the
 * only transitions are the <Link> hover/focus color shifts already owned by the
 * primitive. (Task §24 is stricter than 03 §Motion's permissive language; the
 * stricter, explicit instruction wins.)
 *
 * Breakpoints (task §21 / task 1D): the 8/4 desktop split activates at xl
 * (80rem / 1280px), NOT lg — at 1024–1279px the copy would be too cramped for
 * a side-by-side support column, so laptop stays a comfortable full-width
 * single column. The support statement follows below the CTA group below xl.
 * (Task §21 overrides 03 §Mobile's 48rem split point for the hero; task 1D
 * pushes the split from lg to xl on evidence that lg is too early.) Mobile/
 * tablet (<80rem): single reading column, content-driven panel height.
 *
 * CSS: scoped <style> with var() tokens only (the correct home for complex
 * art-direction — tailwind-v4 §scoped-styles). Logical properties only
 * (FND-I18N-13). class passthrough is layout-only (FND-UI-06). No raw hex,
 * no raw rgba, no brand-font literals (FND-THEME-09 / task §31).
 */
import { Image } from "astro:assets";
import PageContainer from "../../foundation/ui/PageContainer.astro";
import Link from "../../foundation/ui/Link.astro";
import type { HomepageHeroProps } from "./HomepageHero.types.ts";

type Props = HomepageHeroProps;

const {
  title,
  description,
  primaryAction,
  secondaryAction,
  supportText,
  image,
  imageAlt = "",
  locale,
  class: className,
} = Astro.props;

const titleId = "homepage-hero-title";
const hasSupport = Boolean(supportText);
// Alt contract: empty alt = decorative atmosphere (alt="" + role="presentation")
// — the H1 carries the meaning. Non-empty = informative image with that alt.
// The title is never copied into alt (imagery-art-direction §19; task §25).
const isDecorative = imageAlt === "";
---

<section class:list={["homepage-hero", className]} aria-labelledby={titleId}>
  <PageContainer>
    <div class="homepage-hero__panel" data-hero-panel>
      {/* Full-bleed S-Class background (blueprint §7). Decorative atmosphere
          behind the H1/copy but the page LCP — so eager + fetchpriority="high"
          + responsive widths/sizes. object-cover; object-position biases the
          subject so the left copy keeps negative space (asset-specific crop,
          reviewed per breakpoint — task §13). */}
      <Image
        class="homepage-hero__image"
        src={image}
        alt={imageAlt}
        role={isDecorative ? "presentation" : undefined}
        loading="eager"
        fetchpriority="high"
        widths={[480, 768, 1024]}
        sizes="(min-width: 80rem) 80rem, 100vw"
      />

      {/* Controlled directional overlay (03 §Surface/image): stronger behind
          the left copy, controlled behind the right statement, with a bottom
          settle so overlaid text keeps WCAG 2.2 AA contrast at every crop.
          Built ONLY from --color-background via color-mix (the repo scrim
          convention — no raw rgba, no gold, no glow). Decorative (aria-hidden). */}
      <div class="homepage-hero__scrim" aria-hidden="true"></div>

      <div class="homepage-hero__inner">
        <div
          class:list={[
            "homepage-hero__content",
            hasSupport && "homepage-hero__content--split",
          ]}
        >
          <div class="homepage-hero__copy">
            <h1 id={titleId} class="homepage-hero__title">{title}</h1>
            {description ? (
              <p class="homepage-hero__desc">{description}</p>
            ) : null}

            <div class="homepage-hero__actions">
              <Link
                variant="cta"
                to={primaryAction.to}
                href={primaryAction.href}
                locale={locale}
              >
                {primaryAction.label}
              </Link>
              {secondaryAction ? (
                <Link
                  variant="button"
                  to={secondaryAction.to}
                  href={secondaryAction.href}
                  locale={locale}
                >
                  {secondaryAction.label}
                </Link>
              ) : null}
            </div>
          </div>

          {hasSupport ? (
            <aside class="homepage-hero__support">
              <p class="homepage-hero__support-text">{supportText}</p>
            </aside>
          ) : null}
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </PageContainer>
</section>

<style>
  /* --- Panel: the contained cinematic feature panel ----------------------
     One rounded silhouette (--radius-section, 16px) clipping the full-bleed
     image to the corners. A neutral elevated surface shows through while the
     eager image loads (no broken-tile flash). isolation:isolate contains the
     absolute children's stacking order. Mobile-first: content-driven height
     (min 38rem), never a forced desktop ratio, never 100vh (task §15). */
  .homepage-hero__panel {
    position: relative;
    overflow: hidden;
    border-radius: var(--radius-section);
    background: var(--color-surface-elevated);
    isolation: isolate;
    min-block-size: 38rem;
  }

  /* Full-bleed image: fills the entire panel surface, edge to edge inside the
     16px radius. object-cover preserves the crop without distortion. The
     subject is biased toward the right so the left copy keeps negative space
     (blueprint §7 — preserve the car as focal subject). z-index:0 anchors it
     beneath the overlay + content. */
  .homepage-hero__image {
    position: absolute;
    inset: 0;
    inline-size: 100%;
    block-size: 100%;
    object-fit: cover;
    object-position: 70% center;
    z-index: 0;
  }

  /* Controlled directional overlay. Derived ONLY from --color-background via
     color-mix with transparent (the repo scrim convention — ServiceCard /
     SiteHeader) — no black rgba, no gold, no raw hex. Stronger behind the left
     copy (≈92% background), controlled across the right statement (≈60%), plus
     a soft bottom settle so the support statement and CTAs keep AA contrast.
     Decorative (aria-hidden). */
  .homepage-hero__scrim {
    position: absolute;
    inset: 0;
    z-index: 1;
    background:
      linear-gradient(
        90deg,
        color-mix(in oklab, var(--color-background), transparent 8%) 0%,
        color-mix(in oklab, var(--color-background), transparent 24%) 42%,
        color-mix(in oklab, var(--color-background), transparent 40%) 100%
      ),
      linear-gradient(
        0deg,
        color-mix(in oklab, var(--color-background), transparent 18%) 0%,
        transparent 50%
      );
  }

  /* Inner content shell: the grid context for content placement. Padding
     clamp(1.5rem, 4vw, 4rem) (03 §Inner padding). align-items:end grounds the
     content toward the lower/optical region (blueprint §7 / task §19). The
     block-end padding is intentionally generous so the <Link> focus ring
     (outline 2px + offset 2px) is never clipped by the panel's
     overflow:hidden corners (WCAG 2.2 SC 2.4.11 — ServiceCard pattern). */
  .homepage-hero__inner {
    position: relative;
    z-index: 2;
    inline-size: 100%;
    block-size: 100%;
    display: grid;
    align-items: end;
    padding: clamp(1.5rem, 4vw, 4rem);
  }

  /* Content grid: single column by default; 8fr/4fr split (left copy / right
     support statement) at xl only (03 §Desktop content grid, rebalanced per
     task 1E so the copy keeps usable width and the support stays a narrow,
     restrained column — not a large panel). This is CONTENT-PLACEMENT only —
     the image fills the whole panel behind, there is no separate image column
     (blueprint §7 / blueprint-to-ui §18). */
  .homepage-hero__content {
    display: grid;
    gap: var(--space-8);
    align-items: end;
  }
  .homepage-hero__copy {
    display: grid;
    gap: var(--space-5);
    max-inline-size: 38rem;
  }

  /* H1: semantic h1 role, active Theme V2 heading font (--font-heading —
     Inter Tight, a variable face with the full weight range). Explicit
     --font-weight-regular (400) overrides the UA bold default — the hero
     title stays a controlled regular, not heavy/bold (task §8 — avoid
     newspaper ultra-light and marketing extra-bold extremes). Left-aligned,
     tight leading, heading tracking, primary cream. max-inline-size keeps it
     ~2–3 controlled lines (blueprint §7 — ideally ~2 desktop lines); never
     display-scale, never theatrical (task §6).

     RESPONSIVE SIZING (task 1C): a component-local clamp references semantic
     type tokens — floor --text-h2, slope 5vw, cap --text-h1 — so the H1 grows
     smoothly with the viewport WITHOUT touching the global --text-h1 token
     (global tokens stay untouched). At 1440 it is strong (≈4.5rem); at
     1024–1280 laptop it is noticeably smaller (≈3.2–4rem) so it does not wrap
     into a 5-line oversized wall; at mobile it is controlled (floor --text-h2
     ≈2rem). The global --text-h1 stays the cap, so the display max is never
     reached (task §6). */
  .homepage-hero__title {
    margin: 0;
    font-family: var(--font-heading);
    font-weight: var(--font-weight-regular);
    font-size: clamp(var(--text-h2), 5vw, var(--text-h1));
    line-height: var(--line-height-tight);
    letter-spacing: var(--letter-spacing-tight);
    color: var(--color-text-primary);
    max-inline-size: 20ch;
  }

  /* Lede: Manrope, --text-lg, primary cream, controlled measure (≈31rem). */
  .homepage-hero__desc {
    margin: 0;
    max-inline-size: 31rem;
    font-family: var(--font-body);
    font-size: var(--text-lg);
    line-height: var(--line-height-body);
    color: var(--color-text-primary);
  }

  /* CTA group: primary (platinum <Link variant="cta">) + secondary (outlined
     <Link variant="button">). The foundation <Link> owns its own
     accent/hover/focus/44px-target/prefetch treatment — no hero-specific
     button variant, no local .cta classes (03 §Colors / task §8). May wrap or
     stack on narrow widths. */
  .homepage-hero__actions {
    display: flex;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
    gap: var(--space-3);
  }

  /* Right-side support statement (blueprint §7 / 03 §Desktop): small,
     restrained, operational, calm — a quiet muted text block with a subtle
     divider, not cards/stats/badges/icons. Bottom-aligned toward the
     lower-right region; max measure ≈28rem. The divider switches from
     block-start (mobile) to inline-start (desktop) below. */
  .homepage-hero__support {
    align-self: end;
    max-inline-size: 28rem;
  }
  .homepage-hero__support-text {
    margin: 0;
    font-family: var(--font-body);
    font-size: var(--text-base);
    line-height: var(--line-height-body);
    color: var(--color-text-muted);
  }

  /* ── Below xl (<80rem): single column, content-driven height. The support
     statement follows below the CTA group in DOM order; the divider becomes a
     block-start rule. (task 1D — laptop stays a single column, so the copy
     keeps the full panel width instead of a cramped two-column text.) */
  @media (max-width: 79.99rem) {
    .homepage-hero__support {
      border-block-start: 1px solid var(--color-divider);
      padding-block-start: var(--space-5);
    }
  }

  /* ── xl (>=80rem): 8/4 content split. The split activates at xl (1280px)
     rather than lg so laptop (1024–1279px) stays a comfortable full-width
     single column instead of cramped two-column text (task 1D). Panel height
     is content-safe: a cinematic min-block-size floor (the base 38rem, which
     is already ≥ the 03 §Desktop 32–35rem range) and NO restrictive
     max-block-size / aspect-ratio — when the H1 wraps to more lines the panel
     GROWS to fit content instead of clipping the CTA row (task 1B). Still not
     100vh (task §15); still cinematic (the full-bleed image re-crops via
     object-cover as the panel grows). */
  @media (min-width: 80rem) {
    .homepage-hero__content--split {
      grid-template-columns: 8fr 4fr;
      gap: clamp(2rem, 5vw, 5rem);
    }
    .homepage-hero__support {
      padding-inline-start: var(--space-5);
      border-inline-start: 1px solid var(--color-divider);
    }
  }
</style>
